      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Seneca Lake watershed generated $862.2 million in direct tourism spending in 2024, nearly one-fifth of the Finger Lakes region total.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://senecalake.org/tourism-and-economic-data/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Tourism spending in the watershed includes $303.5 million on lodging, $292.1 million on food and beverage, and $94.5 million on retail and services.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://senecalake.org/tourism-and-economic-data/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The watershed supports 55,418 jobs, produces $4.6 billion in visitor spending annually, and saves households $659 per year in taxes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://senecalake.org/tourism-and-economic-data/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "More than 500 campsites across two campgrounds let visitors enjoy the lake’s shoreline, while a full‑service marina offers boat sales, rentals, and supplies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitguernseycounty.com/things-to-do/seneca-lake/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The lake’s clean water is essential not only for recreation but also for the region’s agriculture, where dairy dominates and farms rely on the watershed’s water quality.",
